WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.992
This query reads the patient-admission summary view.

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:07.327
Consumers do not need to repeat the join or stay-duration expression.

00:00:07.327 --> 00:00:10.102
The view already defines that interface.

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:12.452
Run it and identify the grain.

00:00:12.452 --> 00:00:18.582
One row represents one admission with selected patient attributes and a derived stay duration.

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:23.757
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:30.092
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:30.092 --> 00:00:32.602
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:38.807
In a real setting such as a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption,

00:00:38.807 --> 00:00:44.927
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:44.927 --> 00:00:47.207
before discussing syntax.

00:00:47.207 --> 00:00:53.520
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
